        "title": "Feature health decoupled from runtime evidence",
        "summary": "The observability stack now distinguishes user-facing capabilities from the runtime that produced each check, giving the status dashboard a more honest read on what's actually proven green.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Status checks now declare a runtime environment (production-api, desktop-release, local-dev) alongside the feature they cover, so the dashboard groups by feature and labels the runtime per row instead of conflating the two.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "6b9c8b0786777e2fbb7442179a1f5253a441fbd9"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Media Generation health now treats the desktop-release lane as the required proof and the production-auth stream as informational, reflecting that the bundled harness only exists on desktop.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "6b9c8b0786777e2fbb7442179a1f5253a441fbd9"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Desktop release probes on nightly and stable workflows added an image-generation-stream check and now stamp AURA_STATUS_RUNTIME_ENVIRONMENT so artifacts carry runtime provenance.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "6b9c8b0786777e2fbb7442179a1f5253a441fbd9"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          }
        ]
      },
